window.__CAPS = [[0.35, 6.82, "Project controls is the discipline\nthat turns intent into delivery."], [6.82, 16.78, "Planning, cost, earned value, forecasting,\nrisk and project finance \u2014 practised as one\nintegrated whole, not as separate techniques."], [17.4, 24.85, "Project management has PMI.\nAccountancy has ACCA. Finance has CFA."], [24.85, 30.28, "Project controls has had no equivalent \u2014 no\nshared standard, and no professional home."], [30.9, 38.28, "And the discipline is changing. Schedules, forecasts\nand cost reports are increasingly supported by AI."], [38.28, 46.04, "It can accelerate analysis. It can also create false\nconfidence. Technology does not remove accountability."], [46.66, 57.07, "PCI AI exists to close that gap: to give\nproject controls a shared standard, an\nindependent credential and a professional home."], [57.07, 63.05, "Built for how the discipline is practised\nnow, with AI governance at its core."], [63.67, 73.93, "Its mission is to advance the profession through\ncertification, research, professional development,\nstandards, publications and the responsible adoption\nof AI."], [74.55, 81.59, "Its position on that adoption is\nexplicit. It certifies professionals\nwho govern AI \u2014 not who defer to it."], [82.21, 90.43, "The framework is the PCI AI Project\nLeadership Certification Suite \u2014\nthree AI-era leadership credentials."], [91.05, 103.17, "PCL-AI, for project controls. PFL-AI, for\nproject finance. PML-AI, for project management."], [103.17, 106.09, "Finance intelligently. Control\npredictively. Deliver successfully."], [106.71, 109.97, "Each credential rests on a\npublished Body of Knowledge."], [109.97, 116.76, "Its first edition defines thirteen\ndomains and sixty-one knowledge\nareas, weighted forty, forty, twenty."], [117.38, 122.11, "Project accounting and finance. Project\nmanagement principles. And governed AI."], [122.11, 132.24, "AI is not an appendix. It is a domain in its own\nright, and it is embedded through the other twelve."], [132.86, 135.1, "The examination is scenario-based\nand criterion-referenced."], [135.1, 147.93, "It asks whether you can read a cost position,\ninterpret an earned-value index, judge a risk\nresponse, and decide whether an AI-generated forecast\ncan be trusted."], [148.55, 153.58, "There are two routes in \u2014 an experience route\nfor practitioners, and a Foundation route."], [153.58, 162.62, "The credential renews on a three-year CPD\ncycle with a mandatory AI-currency component,\nand every credential can be verified publicly."], [163.24, 173.67, "The discipline is the same wherever\ncapital is deployed at scale, so the\ncredential is written to travel."], [173.67, 181.22, "Energy and utilities. Rail and\ntransportation. Aerospace and defence. Oil\nand gas. Construction and infrastructure."], [181.22, 186.53, "Aviation. Manufacturing. Data centres.\nSmart cities. And government programmes."], [187.15, 196.29, "For organisations, the same standard supports team\nenrolment at scale through corporate programmes, and\ncurriculum alignment through university partnerships."], [196.91, 211.92, "PCI is candid about what it is not.\nIt is not accredited by ANAB, IAS, or\nany ISO/IEC 17024 accreditation body."], [211.92, 216.5, "Its framework is developed with reference\nto those personnel-certification\nprinciples, and it says so plainly."], [216.5, 224.66, "For a body whose value rests on trust, that\nrestraint is the foundation \u2014 not a weakness."], [225.28, 227.59, "AI proposes. The professional disposes."], [227.59, 232.04, "Discover PCI AI at pciai.org"]];
